Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.90,0:00:03.07,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,只问一个问题，远远不够\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}One question is never enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.39,0:00:06.40,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,现实中的分析者会自适应地问很多个\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Real analysts ask many, adaptively,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.40,0:00:09.05,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个都是看了前面的答案才选的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}each chosen after seeing earlier answers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.37,0:00:12.45,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,比如某个桶冒出尖峰，就放大看看\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Maybe you spot a spike in one bin, and zoom in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.70,0:00:15.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原文的定理 1 处理的就是这个\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The paper's Theorem 1 handles this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.41,0:00:19.92,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,看整份 transcript（交互历史）：把它的概率一步一步写成乘积\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Write the probability of the whole transcript, as a product, step by step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.24,0:00:24.20,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,分析者怎么选下一个问题，在两个世界里都一样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The analyst's choice of the next question is the same in both worlds,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.20,0:00:28.70,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以在比值里会约掉，每个答案只剩一个拉普拉斯比值\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so in the ratio it cancels, leaving one Laplace ratio per answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.02,0:00:33.52,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,懂强化学习的话，这就是算轨迹概率比时的那个 trick\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}If you know reinforcement learning, this is the trajectory-ratio trick:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.52,0:00:37.98,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,凡是两个世界里相同的都约掉，每一步的对数比值相加\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}whatever is identical in both worlds cancels, and the per-step log ratios add up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.22,0:00:44.30,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以隐私损失会累加，ε 就像一笔隐私预算，privacy budget\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}So privacy losses add up, and ε behaves like a budget.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.62,0:00:49.14,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个答案花掉一部分；一旦花完，数据管理者就不答了\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each answer spends part of it; once it is spent, the curator stops.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.46,0:00:52.19,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这就回应了 Dinur 和 Nissim\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That is the answer to Dinur and Nissim:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.19,0:00:55.35,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,预算让提问的上限变得明确、可度量\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the budget makes the limit on questions explicit and measurable.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.90,0:01:00.01,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,现在你可以自己算算能省多少噪声\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}You can now compute a real saving yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.33,0:01:05.03,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,暂停一下：直方图有 d 个桶，总预算是 ε\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pause: a histogram with d bins, total budget ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.35,0:01:09.56,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶单独算一个 counting query（计数查询），预算平均分配\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Treat each bin as its own counting query and split the budget evenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.88,0:01:11.69,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶要加多大的噪声？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}How much noise does each bin get?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.53,0:01:29.95,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶分到 1/d 的预算，噪声尺度就是 d/ε\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each bin gets 1/d of the budget, so noise of scale d/ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.27,0:01:33.82,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,把整个直方图当成一个敏感度为 2 的 query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Treated as one query with sensitivity 2,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.82,0:01:37.61,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个桶就都是 2/ε，不管 d 是多少\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}each bin gets 2/ε, whatever d is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.93,0:01:40.52,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,早先的 SuLQ 框架分析得更细\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The earlier framework's sharper analysis
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.52,0:01:44.10,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,把噪声降到大约根号 d，但还是随 d 增大\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}got this down to about √d, but it still grew with d.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.43,0:01:48.06,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,敏感度的用处远不止 counting query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Sensitivity reaches far beyond counts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.38,0:01:50.19,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原文举了三个例子\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Three examples from the paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.88,0:01:56.12,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第一，想象一个社交网络，每条可能的边都是数据库里的一条记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}First, picture a social network where each possible link is one row of the database.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.44,0:02:00.04,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,至少要切断多少条边，才能把网络一分为二？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}How many links must you cut to split the network in two?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.36,0:02:05.68,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这个最小割在改动一条边时最多变化 1，所以敏感度是 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That minimum cut moves by at most 1 when one link changes, so it is 1-sensitive.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.00,0:02:11.06,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一般来说，凡是“至少要改动多少条记录，才能让某件事成立”\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}In general, any question of the form, how many rows would you have to change to make something true,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.06,0:02:13.31,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这类问题，敏感度都是 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}has sensitivity 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.55,0:02:17.61,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第二：如果一个算法读到每条记录的概率都很小\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Second: if an algorithm that rarely looks at any particular row,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.61,0:02:20.20,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,比如只看一个小规模随机样本\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}like one working from a small random sample,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.20,0:02:24.17,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,而且大多数时候都能把 f 近似到 σ 以内\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}approximates f to within σ most of the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.17,0:02:26.39,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,在每个数据库上都是这样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}on every database,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.39,0:02:29.52,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,那么 f 的敏感度最多是两倍 σ\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}then f has sensitivity at most 2σ.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.84,0:02:31.12,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这就是引理 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That is Lemma 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.17,0:02:33.65,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第三，答案不一定是一个数\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Third, the answer need not be a number:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.65,0:02:39.58,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个排名、一个集合、一个比特串，凡是答案之间能定义距离的都行\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}a ranking, a set, a string of bits, anything with a distance between answers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.90,0:02:45.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,选中某个输出的概率，随它到真实答案的距离呈指数衰减\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pick an output with probability that decays exponentially with its distance from the true answer,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.11,0:02:48.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,速率是 ε 除以两倍敏感度\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}at a rate of ε over twice the sensitivity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.43,0:02:53.44,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对比特串来说，这就是每个比特以略低于 1/2 的概率翻转\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}For bit strings, that flips each bit with probability a little below 1/2:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.44,0:02:56.92,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,又是 Warner 的硬币，这次用在了答案上\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Warner's coin again, applied to the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.77,0:03:01.97,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,来看这篇 paper 的最后一部分\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Now the last part of the paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.29,0:03:07.17,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,统计学家和数据挖掘研究者传统上偏爱非交互式模型\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Statisticians and data miners traditionally prefer the non-interactive model:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.17,0:03:12.04,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,数据只做一次隐私处理，发布出去，谁想算什么都行\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}sanitize the data once, publish it, and let anyone compute anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.36,0:03:14.40,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,在这个定义下，行得通吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Can that work under this definition?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.65,0:03:16.72,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原文证明了一个惊人的局限\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The paper proves a striking limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.04,0:03:19.93,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,假设每条记录都是一个 d 位的比特串\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Let each row be a string of d bits.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.25,0:03:23.32,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这里有一族简单的 counting query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Here is a family of simple counting queries:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.32,0:03:27.53,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,给每条记录一个自己的 mask（掩码），也就是一组比特位置\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}give each row its own mask, a subset of bit positions,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.53,0:03:31.49,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,统计有多少条记录在自己的 mask 内有奇数个 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and count the rows with an odd number of ones inside their mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.81,0:03:34.44,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个 query 的敏感度都是 1\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each query has sensitivity 1,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.44,0:03:40.12,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以交互式的管理者回答任意一个，噪声只要 1/ε 左右\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so an interactive curator can answer any one of them with noise of about 1/ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.35,0:03:44.30,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,但一次性发布必须同时为所有 query 做好准备\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}But a one-shot release must prepare for all of them at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.62,0:03:48.29,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,定理 3 表明，对其中至少 2/3 的 query\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Theorem 3 shows that for at least 2/3 of these queries,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.29,0:03:51.36,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,两个随机数据库的发布结果几乎一样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the release looks almost the same for a random database
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.36,0:03:56.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个里每条记录的 mask 内都有偶数个 1，真实答案为 0\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}where every row has even parity, true answer 0,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.11,0:04:00.10,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,另一个里每条记录都有奇数个 1，真实答案为 n\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}as for one where every row is odd, true answer n.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.42,0:04:06.01,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,这已经是最大的差别了，却根本看不出来，除非数据库大到指数级\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The most extreme difference possible, and it cannot be seen, unless the database is exponentially large:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.01,0:04:11.17,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,粗略地说，每条记录每多 4 个比特，需要的记录数就翻一倍\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}roughly, every 4 extra bits per row doubles the rows you would need.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.42,0:04:12.48,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,暂停想一想\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pause and ponder:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.48,0:04:17.21,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,分析者就不能把这些 query 也都拿去问交互式的管理者吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}couldn't an analyst just ask the interactive curator all of these queries too?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.05,0:04:29.88,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,不行：预算会用光\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}No: the budget would run out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.20,0:04:35.55,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,管理者只需回答真正有人问的那几个问题，而且是后来才选的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The curator only has to answer the few questions someone actually asks, chosen later.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.87,0:04:38.72,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,发布的结果没法预知会是哪几个\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}A published release cannot know which few those will be,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.72,0:04:41.76,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以必须同时为所有问题做好准备\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so it must be ready for all of them at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.08,0:04:44.01,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一次性发布就败在这里\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}That is where it breaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.25,0:04:46.33,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,证明思路用到两个事实\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The proof idea uses two facts.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.65,0:04:51.21,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,差分隐私要求：发布结果对每种记录几乎一视同仁\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Privacy forces the release to treat every possible row almost alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.53,0:04:56.80,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,而随机的 mask 把所有记录分成两半，像椒盐一样混在一起\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}And a random mask splits all rows into two halves mixed like salt and pepper,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.80,0:05:00.28,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,所以偶数那一半就像对全体的随机抽样\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}so the even half is like a random poll of everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.60,0:05:04.38,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,接着是链式 trick：从完全随机的记录出发\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Then the chain trick: start from completely random rows,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.38,0:05:08.16,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一条一条地换成 mask 内有偶数个 1 的记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and swap them one at a time for even ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.48,0:05:11.02,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每次替换对输出几乎没影响\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Each swap barely moves the output,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.02,0:05:14.68,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,除非 n 极大，n 次加起来也几乎没影响\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and unless n is huge, all n swaps together barely move it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.00,0:05:20.01,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,换成奇数记录也一样，所以两个数据库看起来都像随机记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The same goes for odd rows, so both databases look like random rows.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.25,0:05:23.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Warner 的硬币，也就是随机响应\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Warner's coin, randomized response,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.09,0:05:27.74,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每个人自己扰动自己的记录，所以谁手里都没有原始数据\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}where each person scrambles their own row so nobody holds the raw data,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.74,0:05:29.35,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,它的局限还要更大\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}is even more limited.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.67,0:05:33.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,命题 2：即使每条记录都用同一个 mask\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Proposition 2: even when every row uses the same mask,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.11,0:05:37.10,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对大多数 mask，它也估计不出奇数记录的个数\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}for most masks it cannot estimate the odd count
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.10,0:05:40.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,除非 n 大到指数级。注意量词\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}unless n is exponentially large. Careful with the quantifiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.41,0:05:44.83,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对任何一个事先就知道的 query，一次性发布都能答好\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}For any one query known in advance, a one-shot release can answer it well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.15,0:05:49.06,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,除非数据库大到指数级，否则单单一次发布\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}What is impossible, unless the database is exponentially large,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.06,0:05:53.15,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,不可能既满足差分隐私，又答好其中的大多数\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}is one private release that answers most of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.47,0:05:57.44,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,结论是：想对各种问题都答得准，又要强隐私\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The lesson: for broad, flexible accuracy with strong privacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.44,0:06:00.08,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就让可信的管理者留在回路里\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}keep the curator in the loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.73,0:06:05.01,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,回到地图上，看看这篇 paper 的后续发展\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Back to our map, to see what grew from this paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.33,0:06:10.23,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,同一年，Dwork 的特邀论文标题就叫《Differential Privacy》\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The same year, in an invited paper titled simply Differential Privacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.23,0:06:12.78,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,给这个领域起了沿用至今的名字\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Dwork introduced the name the field still uses.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.10,0:06:18.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,同年她与 Kenthapadi、McSherry、Mironov 和 Naor 合作\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Another 2006 paper, with Kenthapadi, McSherry, Mironov and Naor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.09,0:06:22.38,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,在另一篇 paper 里引入了一个极小的松弛量 δ\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}added a tiny slack, δ.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.70,0:06:26.11,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,还记得高斯噪声的比值在尾部冲出带外吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Remember the Gaussian whose ratio escaped the band in the tails?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.43,0:06:30.46,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,δ 来替罕见的尾部买单，钟形曲线就回来了\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}δ pays for those rare tails, and lets the bell curve back in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.70,0:06:35.51,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,给每个可能的答案打分，成了 McSherry 和 Talwar 的指数机制\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Scoring every possible answer became McSherry and Talwar's exponential mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.83,0:06:38.58,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,隐私预算发展成了一套组合定理\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The privacy budget grew into a theory of composition,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.58,0:06:42.82,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Dwork、Rothblum 和 Vadhan 还带来了一个惊喜\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}with a surprise from Dwork, Rothblum and Vadhan:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.82,0:06:48.51,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,只要允许那个极小的 δ，k 个问题的总损失就只按根号 k 增长\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}allow that tiny δ, and the total loss of k questions grows only like the square root of k.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.75,0:06:53.49,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Warner 的硬币，也就是第 4 节里证明局限最大的那个模型\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Warner's coin, the model Section 4 showed is most limited,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.49,0:06:56.08,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,正是今天所说的本地化差分隐私\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}is what we now call local differential privacy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.08,0:07:00.50,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,Google 用在 Chrome 浏览器里，苹果用在 iPhone 上\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}used by Google in Chrome and by Apple on iPhones.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.82,0:07:03.50,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,为什么偏偏是局限最大的这个模型？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Why the weakest model?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.82,0:07:06.42,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,原始数据不用托付给任何人\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Nobody has to be trusted with the raw data,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.42,0:07:10.80,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,用户上百万时，几个简单的统计量也扛得住噪声\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and with millions of users, a few simple statistics can afford the noise.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.05,0:07:16.66,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,2016 年，Abadi 和合作者让差分隐私深度学习真正可行\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}In 2016, Abadi and colleagues made it practical to train deep networks privately:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.66,0:07:19.28,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对每个样本的梯度做 clip（梯度裁剪）\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}clip each example's gradient,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.28,0:07:23.18,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就像我们的收入上限，从而限制了敏感度\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}like our income cap, which bounds its sensitivity;
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.18,0:07:27.28,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,加上高斯噪声；并在成千上万步里跟踪预算\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}add Gaussian noise; and track the budget over thousands of steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.60,0:07:31.30,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,用病人数据训练模型的话，这就是你的切入点\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}If you train models on patient data, this is your entry point.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.62,0:07:34.41,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,训练好的网络不过是又一个 f(x)\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}A trained network is just another f(x),
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.41,0:07:37.35,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,问“某个病人在不在训练集里”的攻击\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and attacks that ask whether a patient was in the training set
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.35,0:07:40.47,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就是我们那个做减法的攻击的放大版\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}are our subtraction attack, scaled up.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.70,0:07:43.21,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,还有 2020 年的人口普查\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}And for the 2020 census,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.21,0:07:47.69,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,美国人口普查局用差分隐私保护了公开发布的表\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}the US Census Bureau protected its published tables with differential privacy;
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.69,0:07:51.57,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,只有少数几项，比如各州人口，是精确的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}only a few counts, like state populations, were exact.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.89,0:07:53.49,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,但这是一次性发布\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}But that is a one-shot release.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.64,0:07:57.49,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,暂停想一想：这和第 4 节证明的局限矛盾吗？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Pause and ponder: does Section 4 forbid it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.33,0:08:07.33,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,不矛盾\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.38,0:08:12.92,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,人口普查局的发布，是针对一组事先选定的固定表格量身定制的\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}The Census tuned its release for a fixed set of tables chosen in advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.24,0:08:15.87,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第 4 节排除的只是这样一种发布\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Section 4 only rules out one release
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.87,0:08:18.57,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,对一大类问题里的大多数都答得准\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}that is accurate for most of a huge family of questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.90,0:08:23.34,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,我们来回顾一下\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Let's recap.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.39,0:08:27.14,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第一，隐私指的是：改动任何一个人的记录\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}One: privacy means changing any one person's row
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.14,0:08:31.21,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,任何输出的概率之比最多是 e^ε\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}changes the probability of any output by at most a factor of e^ε.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.53,0:08:36.68,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第二，query 的敏感度，就是一条记录最多能让答案变化多少\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Two: a query's sensitivity is the most one row can change its answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.00,0:08:41.73,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第三，尺度为敏感度除以 ε 的拉普拉斯噪声\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Three: Laplace noise with scale sensitivity/ε
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.73,0:08:46.88,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,就能让它满足差分隐私，数据库再大，误差也不会变大\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}makes it private, with error that does not grow with the database.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.20,0:08:50.30,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第四，一张满足差分隐私的公开表\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Four: one private published table
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.30,0:08:55.39,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,答不好大多数简单的奇偶 query，除非数据库大到指数级\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}cannot answer most simple parity counts unless the database is exponentially large.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.03,0:09:00.60,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,最后留几道题给大家自测，每道题后面都可以暂停一下\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Some questions to test yourself; pause after each.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.92,0:09:05.46,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第一题：n 个 0 到 1 之间的数，平均值的敏感度是多少？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}First: what is the sensitivity of the average of n numbers between 0 and 1?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.70,0:09:18.83,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第二题：在一个医学影像数据集里，每个病人贡献 50 张切片\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Second: in a medical imaging dataset, each patient contributes 50 slices,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.83,0:09:21.91,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,每张切片的梯度都 clip 到 C 以内\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}and each slice's gradient is clipped to size C.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.23,0:09:25.29,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,一个病人能让梯度之和改变多少？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}How much can one patient change the summed gradient?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.53,0:09:39.76,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,第三题：为什么中位数会给拉普拉斯机制带来麻烦？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Third: why does the median give the Laplace mechanism trouble?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.08,0:09:42.85,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,答案和更多练习，都在配套笔记里\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Answers, and more exercises, are in the companion notes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.10,0:09:56.70,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,下次有人说数据集匿名化了，所以很安全，你就知道真正该问的是\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}Next time someone says a dataset is safe because it is anonymized, you will know the better questions:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.70,0:10:01.17,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,用的是多大的 ε，什么才算一个人的一条记录？\N{\fs33\c&H00C8C0B8&\bord1.4}what is the ε, and what counts as one person's row?
